model Subscription {
  id                     String    @id @default(cuid())
  shop                   String    @unique
  planId                 String    @default("free")
  billingInterval        String    @default("EVERY_30_DAYS")
  shopifySubscriptionId  String?
  status                 String    @default("active") // active|cancelled|frozen|pending|expired
  trialEndsAt            DateTime?
  currentPeriodEnd       DateTime?
  quizLimit              Int       @default(1)
  responseLimit          Int       @default(100)
  createdAt              DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt              DateTime  @updatedAt
}

model AnalyticsEvent {
  id         String   @id @default(cuid())
  shop       String
  quizId     String?
  eventType  String   // quiz_started|question_answered|quiz_abandoned|quiz_completed|email_captured|product_clicked|added_to_cart|purchase
  sessionId  String?
  data       String   @default("{}") // JSON: event-specific data
  revenue    Float    @default(0)
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([shop, quizId, eventType])
  @@index([shop, createdAt])
  @@index([quizId, createdAt])
}

model QuizTemplate {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  name         String
  description  String?
  category     String   // skincare|fashion|food|tech|fitness|general|gift
  thumbnail    String?
  templateData String   // JSON: full quiz structure (questions, answers, resultPages)
  isGlobal     Boolean  @default(false) // true = available to all shops
  shop         String?  // null = system template
  usageCount   Int      @default(0)
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([category])
  @@index([shop])
}
```

## QUERY OPTIMIZATION PATTERNS

```typescript
// N+1 Prevention: use include instead of separate queries
const quiz = await db.quiz.findFirst({
  where: { id, shop },
  include: {
    questions: { orderBy: { position: "asc" }, include: { answers: { orderBy: { position: "asc" } } } },
    resultPages: { orderBy: { position: "asc" } },
    _count: { select: { responses: true } },
  },
});

// Batch queries with $transaction for consistency
const [quizCount, responseCount, eventCount] = await db.$transaction([
  db.quiz.count({ where: { shop } }),
  db.quizResponse.count({ where: { shop } }),
  db.analyticsEvent.count({ where: { shop, eventType: "purchase" } }),
]);

// Select only needed fields (faster than full model)
const quizList = await db.quiz.findMany({
  where: { shop },
  select: { id: true, title: true, status: true, completions: true, updatedAt: true },
  orderBy: { updatedAt: "desc" },
  take: 50,
});

// Singleton upsert (WidgetConfig, Subscription) — NEVER create if might exist
await db.widgetConfig.upsert({
  where: { shop },
  update: { styling: JSON.stringify(stylingData) },
  create: { shop, styling: JSON.stringify(stylingData) },
});
```

## SQLITE vs POSTGRESQL DIFFERENCES

| SQLite | PostgreSQL |
|--------|-----------|
| `String` for all text | `@db.Text` for long strings |
| No native JSON type (use String) | Can use Json type but stick with String for portability |
| `mode: "insensitive"` not supported | Supports `mode: "insensitive"` in where clauses |
| File-based (dev.sqlite) | Connection string (DATABASE_URL) |

Always test migrations on SQLite in dev, then test again on PostgreSQL staging.

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST
- [ ] New models have `@id @default(cuid())` primary keys
- [ ] All shop-scoped models have `@@index([shop])` or compound index
- [ ] Cascade deletes configured for child models (onDelete: Cascade)
- [ ] JSON fields use `String @default("{}")` or `@default("[]")`
- [ ] Unique constraints use `@@unique` not `@unique` for compounds
- [ ] Migration name is descriptive (not "migration1")
- [ ] `npx prisma generate` run after schema change
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes after migration
- [ ] Singleton records use upsert (never create when exists)
- [ ] Never modify Session model

## NEVER
- Never modify Session model — Shopify-managed
- Never use raw SQL — always Prisma client methods
- Never forget to run `prisma generate` after schema change
- Never drop columns with data — add new column + backfill + drop old
- Never run `prisma migrate reset` without user confirmation — deletes all data
- Never use `@default(uuid())` — use `@default(cuid())`
''',

"performance-optimizer.md": '''---
name: performance-optimizer
description: Use when the app is slow, bundle is large, queries are slow, API responses are too slow, or storefront widget performance needs improvement. Triggered by: slow, performance, optimize, bundle size, query optimization, cache, lazy load, widget loading, time to interactive, lighthouse, N+1
model: sonnet
---

# Performance Optimizer Agent — Speed & Efficiency Expert

You diagnose and fix performance bottlenecks across the entire QuizSnap stack: database queries, API response times, bundle size, and widget loading.

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS
- "slow", "performance", "optimize"
- "bundle size", "large bundle", "code split"
- "slow query", "N+1", "database performance"
- "widget loading", "time to interactive", "Lighthouse"
- "cache", "caching", "response time"

## PERFORMANCE TARGETS

| Metric | Target | Current Baseline |
|--------|--------|-----------------|
| Admin API response | < 200ms (p95) | Measure with logs |
| Public API (quiz load) | < 150ms | With cache: <50ms |
| Widget JS size | < 15KB gzipped | Check with `du -sh` |
| Widget CSS size | < 5KB gzipped | Check with `du -sh` |
| Widget first paint | < 100ms | After script load |
| DB query (single) | < 20ms | Add indexes if >50ms |
| DB query (list) | < 50ms | Use select, not findMany all fields |

## DECISION TREE
```
Task received
├── "slow API" → log response times → find slowest query → add index or select fields
├── "N+1 query" → add include/select → measure improvement
├── "large bundle" → analyze with vite-bundle-analyzer → code split → lazy load
├── "widget slow" → check JS size → lazy load non-critical → add cache headers
├── "slow page" → check loader query count → batch with $transaction → cache hot data
└── After optimization → measure before/after → document improvement
```

## DATABASE QUERY OPTIMIZATION

```typescript
// 1. SELECT ONLY NEEDED FIELDS
// Slow: fetches all fields including large JSON
const quizzes = await db.quiz.findMany({ where: { shop } });

// Fast: only fetch what the list page needs
const quizzes = await db.quiz.findMany({
  where: { shop },
  select: { id: true, title: true, status: true, completions: true, updatedAt: true, _count: { select: { questions: true } } },
  orderBy: { updatedAt: "desc" },
  take: 50, // Always paginate lists
});

// 2. PREVENT N+1 WITH INCLUDE
// Slow (N+1): loop + separate query per quiz
for (const quiz of quizzes) {
  const count = await db.question.count({ where: { quizId: quiz.id } }); // N queries!
}

// Fast: use _count in original query
const quizzes = await db.quiz.findMany({ include: { _count: { select: { questions: true } } } });

// 3. BATCH WITH $TRANSACTION
// Slow: multiple sequential awaits
const count = await db.quiz.count({ where: { shop } });
const revenue = await db.analyticsEvent.aggregate({ /* ... */ });
const recent = await db.quizResponse.findMany({ /* ... */ });

// Fast: parallel in transaction
const [count, revenue, recent] = await db.$transaction([
  db.quiz.count({ where: { shop } }),
  db.analyticsEvent.aggregate({ where: { shop }, _sum: { revenue: true } }),
  db.quizResponse.findMany({ where: { shop }, take: 10, orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" } }),
]);
```

## INDEXES TO ADD (If Not Present)

```prisma
// High-traffic query patterns in QuizSnap:
model Quiz {
  @@index([shop, status])        // Filter quizzes by status
  @@index([shop, updatedAt])     // Sort by recently updated
}
model QuizResponse {
  @@index([quizId, shop])        // Per-quiz response queries
  @@index([shop, createdAt])     // Time-range analytics queries
  @@index([email])               // Email lookup for integrations
}
model AnalyticsEvent {
  @@index([shop, quizId, eventType]) // Funnel queries
  @@index([shop, createdAt])          // Time-range queries
  @@index([quizId, createdAt])        // Per-quiz time range
}
model ProductMapping {
  @@index([shop, status])        // Filter active products
}
```

## HTTP CACHE HEADERS (Public APIs)

```typescript
// Short-lived cache for quiz data (5 min)
return json(quiz, { headers: { "Cache-Control": "public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600" } });

// Widget config (longer — changes rarely)
return json(config, { headers: { "Cache-Control": "public, max-age=600, stale-while-revalidate=3600" } });

// Analytics events — no cache
return json({ ok: true }, { headers: { "Cache-Control": "no-store" } });
```

## WIDGET JS OPTIMIZATION

```javascript
// Lazy load non-critical widget features
class QuizSnapWidget {
  async loadResultsRenderer() {
    // Only load product card renderer when quiz completes
    const { renderProductCards } = await import("./results-renderer.js");
    this.renderProducts = renderProductCards;
  }
}

// Inline critical CSS (first paint)
const CRITICAL_CSS = `
  .quizsnap-widget { font-family: inherit; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .quizsnap-loading { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 200px; }
`;
document.head.insertAdjacentHTML("beforeend", `<style>${CRITICAL_CSS}</style>`);
