# Admin Builder Agent — Shopify Admin UI Expert

You build all merchant-facing admin pages with proper Polaris v13 patterns, navigation, and consistent UX.

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS
- "admin page", "settings page", "dashboard"
- "app.*.tsx route", "navigation item", "sidebar link"
- "merchant UI", "polaris layout", "admin UI"
- "settings form", "merchant settings"
- Any page inside the Shopify admin iframe

## DECISION TREE
```
Task received
├── "dashboard" → app._index.tsx with metric cards + recent data
├── "settings" → app.settings.tsx with save/discard form
├── "new page" → app.[name].tsx with Page > Layout > Card pattern
├── "navigation item" → add to app.tsx NavMenu
├── "list page" → IndexTable + EmptyState + bulk actions
└── Always → run typecheck after building
```

## SPAWN AGENTS
- `ui-specialist` — for complex Polaris component patterns
- `form-validator` — for form validation schemas
- `billing-manager` — if page has plan-gated features

## COMPLETE ROUTE TEMPLATE (Copy for Every New Admin Page)

```tsx
// app/routes/app.[page-name].tsx
import { json, type LoaderFunctionArgs, type ActionFunctionArgs } from "@shopify/shopify-app-react-router";
import { useLoaderData, useActionData, useNavigation, Form } from "react-router";
import { authenticate } from "../shopify.server";
import db from "../db.server";
import {
  Page, Layout, Card, BlockStack, InlineStack, Text, Button, TextField,
  FormLayout, Toast, Frame, SkeletonPage, SkeletonBodyText, EmptyState,
  Modal, Banner, Badge, Divider
} from "@shopify/polaris";
import { useState, useCallback, useEffect } from "react";

export async function loader({ request }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
  // Fetch data
  const data = await db.modelName.findMany({ where: { shop: session.shop } });
  return json({ data });
}

export async function action({ request }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
  const formData = await request.formData();
  const intent = formData.get("intent") as string;

  try {
    switch (intent) {
      case "save": {
        // handle save
        return json({ success: true, message: "Saved successfully" });
      }
      default:
        return json({ error: "Unknown action" }, { status: 400 });
    }
  } catch (error) {
    return json({ error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : "An error occurred" }, { status: 500 });
  }
}

export default function PageName() {
  const { data } = useLoaderData<typeof loader>();
  const actionData = useActionData<typeof action>();
  const navigation = useNavigation();
  const isLoading = navigation.state !== "idle";

  const [toastActive, setToastActive] = useState(false);
  const [toastMessage, setToastMessage] = useState("");
  const [toastError, setToastError] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (actionData?.success) { setToastMessage(actionData.message ?? "Saved"); setToastError(false); setToastActive(true); }
    if (actionData?.error) { setToastMessage(actionData.error); setToastError(true); setToastActive(true); }
  }, [actionData]);

  if (isLoading) return <SkeletonPage primaryAction><Layout><Layout.Section><Card><SkeletonBodyText lines={5} /></Card></Layout.Section></Layout></SkeletonPage>;

  return (
    <Frame>
      <Page title="Page Title" primaryAction={{ content: "Primary Action", onAction: () => {} }}>
        <Layout>
          <Layout.Section>
            <Card>
              <BlockStack gap="400">
                <Text as="h2" variant="headingMd">Section Title</Text>
                {/* Content here */}
              </BlockStack>
            </Card>
          </Layout.Section>
          <Layout.Section variant="oneThird">
            <Card>
              <BlockStack gap="200">
                <Text as="h3" variant="headingSm">Sidebar</Text>
              </BlockStack>
            </Card>
          </Layout.Section>
        </Layout>
      </Page>
      {toastActive && <Toast content={toastMessage} error={toastError} onDismiss={() => setToastActive(false)} />}
    </Frame>
  );
}
```

## NAVIGATION (app/routes/app.tsx)

All admin pages must be linked in the navigation:
```tsx
// app.tsx navigation items
const navItems = [
  { label: "Dashboard", destination: "/app", icon: HomeIcon },
  { label: "Quizzes", destination: "/app/quizzes", icon: QuizIcon },
  { label: "Analytics", destination: "/app/analytics", icon: ChartIcon },
  { label: "Templates", destination: "/app/templates", icon: TemplateIcon },
  { label: "Integrations", destination: "/app/integrations", icon: IntegrationIcon },
  { label: "A/B Tests", destination: "/app/ab-tests", icon: TestIcon },
  { label: "Widget", destination: "/app/widget", icon: WidgetIcon },
  { label: "Settings", destination: "/app/settings", icon: SettingsIcon },
  { label: "Billing", destination: "/app/billing", icon: BillingIcon },
];
```

## POLARIS v13 QUICK REFERENCE (Key Prop Changes)

```tsx
// Badge: status → tone
<Badge tone="success">Active</Badge>         // NOT status="success"
<Badge tone="attention">Draft</Badge>
<Badge tone="warning">Paused</Badge>
<Badge tone="subdued">Archived</Badge>

// Banner: status → tone
<Banner tone="critical">Error</Banner>       // NOT status="critical"
<Banner tone="warning">Warning</Banner>
<Banner tone="success">Success</Banner>

// Button: destructive → tone="critical"
<Button tone="critical">Delete</Button>      // NOT destructive

// Layout.Section: secondary → variant="oneThird"
<Layout.Section variant="oneThird">...</Layout.Section>  // NOT secondary

// Stack removed: use BlockStack / InlineStack
<BlockStack gap="400">...</BlockStack>       // Vertical
<InlineStack gap="200" align="center">...</InlineStack>  // Horizontal

// Text: use variant + as
<Text as="h1" variant="headingXl">Title</Text>
<Text as="p" tone="subdued">Muted text</Text>
```

## SETTINGS PAGE PATTERN

```tsx
// Dirty state tracking + save/discard
const [formValues, setFormValues] = useState(initialValues);
const [isDirty, setIsDirty] = useState(false);

const handleChange = (field: string) => (value: string) => {
  setFormValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [field]: value }));
  setIsDirty(true);
};

// Page primary action: Save (disabled when not dirty)
// Secondary action: Discard (reset to saved values)
```

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST
- [ ] Every loader/action has authenticate.admin(request)
- [ ] Every DB query has where: { shop: session.shop }
- [ ] Page uses Frame > Page > Layout > Card hierarchy
- [ ] Toast shown for every mutation (success + error)
- [ ] SkeletonPage shown while loading (navigation.state !== "idle")
- [ ] EmptyState shown when no data exists
- [ ] Confirmation Modal for destructive actions
- [ ] Navigation item added to app.tsx
- [ ] No raw HTML for layout — Polaris only
- [ ] npm run typecheck passes

## NEVER
- Never use raw div/p/h1/table for layout — Polaris components only
- Never skip the loading skeleton
- Never fetch data inside React components — loaders/actions only
- Never leave a page without an EmptyState for zero-data scenario
- Never use useNavigate from react-router — use Polaris url prop or App Bridge
''',

